mounted filesystems unless you are sure of the implications.  NFS
has some assumptions about the characteristics of the  file  sys‐
tems  being  exported,  e.g. when timestamps are updated.  Re‐ex‐
porting should work to some extent and can even be useful in some
cases, but don’t expect it works as well as with local file  sys‐
tems.   The  export options are tied to the local mount points in
the kernel and must be non‐contradictory for any exported  subdi‐
rectory  of the local server mount point.  It is recommended that
all exported directories within the  same  server  filesystem  be
specified  on  adjacent  lines  going  down the tree.  You cannot
specify a hostname that is also the name of a netgroup.  Specify‐
ing the full domain specification for  a  hostname  can  normally
circumvent the problem.
